'll give you just  one piece of evidence for that since  we're almost out of time and that is if  you look at the history of Western  countries in the 1960s all of them went  through the exact same metamorphosis and  the same almost at the same moment and  so countries for example like Germany  and Britain that have long had  establishment of religion and official  churches and all the things that the  Americans didn't do all had that exact  same thing there was immediate  institution of no-fault divorce  throughout the Western world in the  1970s in almost every country immediate  institution of barriers on employers and  their freedom of contract with employees  there was a complete collapse of sexual  mores throughout the Western world all  at once whether it's New Zealand  Australia Germany England America this  is not due to the founding fathers I can  assure you of that this is something  where I want to go back to Josh Mitchell  Mitchell to conclude and it's his  comments about Nietzsche's diagnosis and  what's wrong with us that's where you  need to go to understand our current  situation it's a psychological malady  that is profoundly it is a profound  indication of a deep dissatisfaction in  the Western soul now that it has gotten  rid of God it has gotten rid of nature  and reason it has gotten rid of all  meaning in human life it has put us  exactly in the situation he said  Tocqueville worried about where we're  living in the present moment  that's where we are and that is not  something that the founding fathers can  be blamed for and I also agree something  the founding fathers probably can't  solve help us solve that's something  we're gonna have to solve ourselves and  I don't know how to do it either but  thank you very much  I think that's a fitting way to conclude  that's all we have time for our next  session will begin after a short break  thank you  [Applause]
 

